    <string name="health_calc_title">How the baseline is calculated</string>
    <string name="health_calc_window">Your baseline is the average of your valid readings over the 30 days before the day you are looking at. That day is left out, so a reading is never compared with an average it helped to make.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_range">Your usual range is that average plus or minus one standard deviation. The Z badge counts how many standard deviations a reading sits from your average, limited to plus or minus 3.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_calibration">A baseline needs at least 7 valid days. Until then Apex says it is still learning instead of using population averages.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_hrv">Heart rate variability is averaged on a log scale because it changes in proportion, so its range is slightly wider above the average than below.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_floor">Very steady readings get a small minimum spread, so a tiny change cannot look dramatic.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_progress">%1$d of %2$d valid days so far.</string>
    <string name="health_calc_established">Baseline ready, built from %1$d valid days.</string>

